<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns/1.0/graphml.xsd">
  <key id="d6" for="edge" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d5" for="edge" attr.name="keywords" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d4" for="edge" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d3" for="edge" attr.name="weight" attr.type="double" />
  <key id="d2" for="node" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d1" for="node" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d0" for="node" attr.name="entity_type" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;LOUIS I, CARDINAL OF GUISE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Louis I, Cardinal of Guise was the fourth son of Claude, Duke of Guise, and Antoinette de Bourbon, and the younger brother of Charles of Guise, Cardinal of Lorraine, and Mary of Guise, queen consort of King James V of Scotland. He was made Bishop of Troyes in 1545.")</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0437-ddaa09ea00f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLAUDE, DUKE OF GUISE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Claude, Duke of Guise was the father of Louis I, Cardinal of Guise and the elder brother of Charles of Guise, Cardinal of Lorraine, and Mary of Guise, queen consort of King James V of Scotland.")</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0437-ddaa09ea00f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANTOINETTE DE BOURBON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Antoinette de Bourbon was the mother of Louis I, Cardinal of Guise and the wife of Claude, Duke of Guise.")</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0437-ddaa09ea00f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHARLES OF GUISE, CARDINAL OF LORRAINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Charles of Guise, Cardinal of Lorraine was the elder brother of Louis I, Cardinal of Guise and the younger brother of Mary of Guise, queen consort of King James V of Scotland.")</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0437-ddaa09ea00f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MARY OF GUISE, QUEEN CONSORT OF KING JAMES V OF SCOTLAND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mary of Guise, queen consort of King James V of Scotland was the younger sister of Louis I, Cardinal of Guise and Charles of Guise, Cardinal of Lorraine.")</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0437-ddaa09ea00f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARDINAL JEAN DE LORRAINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cardinal Jean de Lorraine was the uncle of Louis I, Cardinal of Guise.")</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0437-ddaa09ea00f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JOINVILLE, CHAMPAGNE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Joinville, Champagne is the birthplace of Louis I, Cardinal of Guise.")</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0437-ddaa09ea00f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PARIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Paris is the place of death of Louis I, Cardinal of Guise.")</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0437-ddaa09ea00f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARDINAL OF GUISE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cardinal of Guise is a person who succeeded his uncle Louis I in some capacity, likely a religious or political position."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0437-ddaa09ea00f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOUIS I&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Louis I is a person who was the uncle of the Cardinal of Guise and held a position that allowed him to be succeeded by his nephew."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0437-ddaa09ea00f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GUISE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Guise likely refers to the family or lineage of the Cardinal of Guise, possibly a noble family or region."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0437-ddaa09ea00f9</data>
    </node>
    <edge source="&quot;CARDINAL OF GUISE&quot;" target="&quot;LOUIS I&quot;">
      <data key="d3">16.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Cardinal of Guise succeeded his uncle Louis I, indicating a familial and possibly hierarchical relationship."</data>
      <data key="d5">"succession, familial relationship"</data>
      <data key="d6">ramdocs-0437-ddaa09ea00f9</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;CARDINAL OF GUISE&quot;" target="&quot;GUISE&quot;">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Guise likely refers to the family or lineage of the Cardinal of Guise."</data>
      <data key="d5">"family lineage, heritage"</data>
      <data key="d6">ramdocs-0437-ddaa09ea00f9</data>
    </edge>
  </graph>
